<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Calivi APT repository</title>
<style>
  :root { --bg: #fafafa; --fg: #1c1c1c; --muted: #666; --code: #efefef; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { :root { --bg: #161616; --fg: #e8e8e8; --muted: #999; --code: #242424; } }
  body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font: 16px/1.55 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 46rem; margin: 2.5rem auto; padding: 0 16px; }
  pre { background: var(--code); padding: .8rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; overflow-x: auto; }
  code { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: .92em; }
  small, .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  a { color: inherit; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Calivi APT repository</h1>
<p>Packages of <a href="https://calivi.ai">Calivi</a> for <b>Debian 13</b> (trixie),
<b>Ubuntu 24.04 LTS</b> (noble) and <b>Ubuntu 26.04 LTS</b> (resolute), amd64. Every package here
was installed and tested in a VM of its distribution before it was published, and a release is
published only when all three passed.</p>

<h2>Install</h2>
<p>From 0.6.2 the package adds this repository itself. Download it for your distribution from the
<a href="https://github.com/orkun-soylu/calivi/releases/latest">latest release</a>
(<code>+deb13</code>, <code>+ubuntu24.04</code> or <code>+ubuntu26.04</code>) and install it once:</p>
<pre><code>sudo apt install ./calivi_X.Y.Z-1+deb13_amd64.deb</code></pre>
<p>From then on <code>apt upgrade</code> updates Calivi like the rest of the system. An upgrade
that lands while a reply is running restarts Calivi only once the reply is done.</p>

<h2>Or add the repository by hand</h2>
<pre><code>curl -fsSL https://apt.calivi.ai/calivi.gpg | sudo tee /usr/share/keyrings/calivi.gpg &gt;/dev/null

# Check the key. Cloud and minimal images have no gpg: sudo apt install gpg
gpg --show-keys /usr/share/keyrings/calivi.gpg   # must show @FPR@

. /etc/os-release
sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/calivi.sources &gt;/dev/null &lt;&lt;EOF
Types: deb
URIs: https://apt.calivi.ai
Suites: $VERSION_CODENAME
Components: main
Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/calivi.gpg
EOF
sudo apt update &amp;&amp; sudo apt install calivi</code></pre>
<p class="muted">This writes the same two files the package installs, so installing the package
later takes them over without a question.</p>

<h2>Signing key</h2>
<p><code>@FPR_SPACED@</code><br>
<small>Calivi APT repository &lt;apt@calivi.ai&gt; · RSA 4096 · <a href="calivi.asc">calivi.asc</a></small></p>

<p class="muted">Source and release notes: <a href="https://github.com/orkun-soylu/calivi">github.com/orkun-soylu/calivi</a>.</p>
</body>
</html>
